// extdeps/memory/sk_hynix.dag — SK Hynix DDR4 module catalog (vendor data authority).
//
// SK Hynix's published DDR4 modules, as std.memory DramModuleCatalogRow values.
// Vendor hardware is an external dependency: it lives in extdeps/, importing the
// catalog SHAPE from std/memory. std/memory owns only the shape + the manufacturer
// taxonomy; it does not enumerate any one vendor's parts. Which specific modules a
// given host is populated with is an operator deployment fact (ctrl), not a fact
// about SK Hynix.
//
// Operator DIMMs: HMA82GR7AFR4N-VK 16GB PC4-21300 @ 2666 MT/s.

module extdeps.memory.sk_hynix

import std.measure { ByteSize, byte_size, bit_width }
import std.memory.types { DramModuleCatalogRow }

// 16 GiB per stick (1×16GB, 2Gx72). The "PC4-21300" / "PC4-2666V" JEDEC class is
// data_rate_mts (2666) × 8 bytes rounded to the label — derivable, so not stored.
data stick_capacity_bytes: ByteSize = byte_size(17179869184)

// HMA82GR7AFR4N-VK, decoded position-by-position from the SK Hynix DDR4 module part
// number — so each axis is a grounded fact, not a marketplace listing label:
//   [H] SK Hynix · [R] 288-pin Registered DIMM (RDIMM) · [7] x72 data width (ECC) ·
//   [4] x4 device organization · [-VK] DDR4-2666 19-19-19 (PC4-21300).
// The two prior rows ("...server_catalog" / "...ecc_reg_single_rank_catalog") were ONE
// JEDEC part under two marketplace listings — collapsed to this single grounded row.
// Anchor: SK Hynix DDR4 module decoder DDR4MODULE_20170623.fm (MODULE TYPE / DATA
//   WIDTH / ORGANIZATION / SPEED fields); rank per datasheet Rev.1.7 ordering table.
data hma82gr7afr4n_vk_catalog: DramModuleCatalogRow = DramModuleCatalogRow {
  part_number: "HMA82GR7AFR4N-VK",
  manufacturer: SkHynix,
  capacity_bytes: stick_capacity_bytes,
  data_rate_mts: 2666,
  ecc: true,
  buffering: Registered,
  chip_width: bit_width(4),
  // rank is NOT a part-number field — derived from the SK Hynix datasheet ordering
  // table (16GB x4 = 1R) and CONFIRMED on live hardware 2026-06-17:
  //   sudo dmidecode --type 17 | grep -E 'Part Number:|Rank:'   → every DIMM Rank: 1
  // on both srv1 (altrad8ud-1l2t-1) and srv2 (alstrad8d-1l2t-2), 8 sticks each.
  // (Do NOT infer rank from the "...R4..." digit — that is device width x4, not rank=4.)
  rank_count: 1,
}
